  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">The main objective of this project is to provide health assistance to vulnerable communities affected by Cholera in the DRC. This WHO project provides medical treatment for patients, trains health personnel, and supports disease surveillance, among other activities. The project provides life-saving humanitarian assistance to 127,952 people, including 27,081 women, 26,019 men, and 74,852 children.</narrative>
  </description>
